---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import { links } from '../links';
---

<Site
	title="Privacy · Reqly"
	description="Reqly keeps your traffic on your Mac. It has no account, no analytics and no tracking."
>
	<article class="prose">
		<h1>Privacy</h1>
		<p class="lead">
			Reqly keeps your traffic on your Mac. It has no account, no analytics and no tracking.
		</p>

		<h2>What the app sends</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>A check for updates,</strong> to GitHub, once a day. Like any web request, it shows
				GitHub your IP address. You can turn it off in Settings.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Requests you send yourself,</strong> to the servers you choose.</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Nothing after a crash,</strong> unless you choose to. Reqly offers to open a GitHub
				issue with the crash report, which you read and edit before you submit it.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>What stays on your Mac</h2>
		<p>
			The traffic you capture, your rules, scripts and settings. Captured traffic is deleted when
			you quit, unless you save it as a session.
		</p>

		<h2>This website</h2>
		<p>
			No cookies and no analytics. The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, which logs visitors' IP
			addresses for security, as GitHub's privacy statement describes.
		</p>

		<h2>Questions</h2>
		<p>Ask on GitHub: <a href={links.issues}>open an issue</a>.</p>
	</article>
</Site>
